Description: Lock the info cache row in instance_info_cache_update
 MariaDB 11.x enables innodb_snapshot_isolation by default (MDEV-26642),
 making InnoDB detect write-write conflicts under REPEATABLE-READ: an
 UPDATE fails with ER_CHECKREAD (1020) when the row was modified by
 another transaction after the current transaction took its snapshot.
 .
 instance_info_cache_update() reads the row then updates it in the same
 transaction, so a concurrent cache update (for example the Neutron vif
 events racing the delete flow) can commit in between. The failing
 UPDATE also discards the nested savepoint, so the savepoint teardown
 raises ER_SAVEPOINT_NOT_EXIST (1305), and that DBError escapes both the
 DBDuplicateEntry handler and wrap_db_retry, leaving the server in
 ERROR state during delete (observed in the OpenStack Debian CI against
 MariaDB 11.8.6).
Author: Thomas Goirand <zigo@debian.org>
Forwarded: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/nova/+/1010847
Last-Update: 2026-10-16

Index: nova/nova/db/main/api.py
===================================================================
--- nova.orig/nova/db/main/api.py
+++ nova/nova/db/main/api.py
@@ -2462,8 +2462,18 @@ def instance_info_cache_update(context,
     """
     convert_objects_related_datetimes(values)
 
+    # NOTE(zigo): Lock the row until the end of the transaction. Since
+    # MariaDB 11.x, innodb_snapshot_isolation is enabled by default and
+    # makes InnoDB abort an UPDATE with ER_CHECKREAD (1020) when the row
+    # was modified by another transaction after this transaction took
+    # its snapshot. The failing statement also discards the savepoint
+    # used below, and the savepoint teardown then fails with
+    # ER_SAVEPOINT_NOT_EXIST (1305), masking the original error. A
+    # locking read serializes concurrent writers instead, which also
+    # prevents the lost update.
     info_cache = model_query(context, models.InstanceInfoCache).\
                      filter_by(instance_uuid=instance_uuid).\
+                     with_for_update().\
                      first()
     needs_create = False
     if info_cache and info_cache['deleted']:
